ed scripts from a role sandbox (2026-10-20). Do not print proxy settings. Record what you installed and where each source came from.\n\nLiterature and venues:\n- arXiv: search with `https://export.arxiv.org/api/query?search_query=...&max_results=N` (Atom; one request every 3 s, faster gets 429); a paper at `https://arxiv.org/abs/<id>`, `/pdf/<id>`, `/html/<id>` (recent papers) and its LaTeX source at `/e-print/<id>`; older papers as HTML at `https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/<id>`.\n- OpenReview: `https://api2.openreview.net/notes/search?term=<title, keywords or forum id>&limit=N` returns submissions, reviews and decisions with their text; its forum pages, PDFs and other API routes ask for a browser challenge, so take a paper's PDF from arXiv.\n- Metadata and open copies: OpenAlex `https://api.openalex.org/works?search=...`; Crossref `https://api.crossref.org/works?query=...`; a DOI's BibTeX with `curl -LH 'Accept: application/x-bibtex' https://doi.org/<doi>`; open-access PDFs from Unpaywall `https://api.unpaywall.org/v2/<doi>?email=<an address>`; Semantic Scholar `https://api.semanticscholar.org/graph/v1/paper/arXiv:<id>?fields=...` (a rate limit shared by all callers: after 429, wait and retry); Hugging Face `https://huggingface.co/api/papers/<arXiv id>`.\n- Proceedings, static pages and PDFs: PMLR `https://proceedings.mlr.press/v<volume>/`; NeurIPS `https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/<year>`; ACL Anthology `https://aclanthology.org/<id>.pdf` and `.bib`; CVF `https://openaccess.thecvf.com/<CONF><year>?day=all`; accepted papers at `https://iclr.cc/virtual/<year>/papers.html`, and the same path on icml.cc and neurips.cc.\n- Life sciences: PubMed through `https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi?db=pubmed&term=...` (then `efetch.fcgi`); Europe PMC `https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=...&format=json`; bioRxiv `https://api.biorxiv.org/details/biorxiv/<doi>`; records and files on Zenodo `https://zenodo.org/api/r